# TTP-2026-0116 — Ivanti Connect Secure Pre-Auth IF-T Overflow to Internal Windows Pivot (SPAWN / CL-UNK-0979)
# XDM modeling-rule paste-buffer (normalization substrate) generated by detection_scanner/scripts/export_artifacts.py

## MODELING RULE — Ivanti Connect Secure Appliance IF-T Telemetry Normalization (XDM normalization substrate)
# raw source dataset: ivanti_ics_raw
# vendor/product: Ivanti / Connect Secure
# XDM fields populated: xdm.source.ipv4, xdm.source.host.hostname, xdm.target.host.hostname, xdm.event.description, xdm.event.outcome, xdm.observer.type
# Normalizes the raw Ivanti Connect Secure appliance debug/syslog stream (ivanti_ics_raw) into addressable XDM fields so the pre-auth IF-T exploitation tell and the attacker source IP become searchable and stitchable. Raw vendor fields map as: source_address -> xdm.source.ipv4, client_hostname -> xdm.source.host.hostname, appliance_hostname -> xdm.target.host.hostname, message -> xdm.event.description, auth_result -> xdm.event.outcome. This modeling rule is the normalization SUBSTRATE beneath the appliance-to-endpoint correlation — it enables firing, it does not itself fire.

[MODEL: dataset = ivanti_ics_raw]
| alter xdm.source.ipv4 = source_address
| alter xdm.source.host.hostname = client_hostname
| alter xdm.target.host.hostname = appliance_hostname
| alter xdm.event.description = message
| alter xdm.event.outcome = auth_result
| alter xdm.observer.type = "vpn-gateway"
| filter xdm.event.description contains "IFT" or xdm.event.description contains "IF-T"

## MODELING RULE — Ivanti Appliance Log-Tampering File-Event Normalization (XDM normalization substrate)
# raw source dataset: ivanti_ics_raw
# vendor/product: Ivanti / Connect Secure
# XDM fields populated: xdm.target.file.path, xdm.target.file.filename, xdm.event.operation, xdm.source.ipv4
# Normalizes the Ivanti appliance file-audit sub-stream so the SPAWNSLOTH log-tampering deletions become addressable XDM file events. Raw vendor fields map as: file_path -> xdm.target.file.path, file_operation -> xdm.event.operation, source_address -> xdm.source.ipv4. Filters to the specific appliance logs the intrusion wipes (log.events.vc0, debuglog) and the emptied /var/cores. Substrate only — enables the defense-evasion detection, does not fire itself.

[MODEL: dataset = ivanti_ics_raw]
| filter event_type = "file_audit"
| alter xdm.target.file.path = file_path
| alter xdm.target.file.filename = arrayindex(split(file_path, "/"), -1)
| alter xdm.event.operation = file_operation
| alter xdm.source.ipv4 = source_address
| filter xdm.target.file.path in ("/data/runtime/logs/log.events.vc0", "/data/var/dlogs/debuglog", "/var/cores")
| filter xdm.event.operation in ("DELETE", "TRUNCATE")

